# Shell scripts are executed inside Linux containers (Docker ENTRYPOINT). A CRLF
# shebang line (`#!/bin/sh\r`) makes the kernel look for a literal `/bin/sh\r`
# interpreter and fail with a misleading "no such file or directory" — this bit a
# local Windows build (core.autocrlf=true, no prior .gitattributes) even though the
# committed blobs and CI (Linux checkout) were never affected.
*.sh text eol=lf
